<title>USA: Avondale Q3 shr falls, prior yr with gains.</title>
<headline>Avondale Q3 shr falls, prior yr with gains.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS, La. 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>		    3 months ended Sept 30  9 months ended Sep 30</p>
<p>				 1996	   1995     1996	1995</p>
<p> Net sales	     $148,384     $148,785 $457,457  $435,148</p>
<p> Cost of sales	  129,336	133,992  402,957   393,131</p>
<p> Gross profit	    19,048	 14,793   54,500    42,017</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>administrative expense</p>
<p>				9,811	  7,958   28,136    23,219</p>
<p>Income from operations  </p>
<p>				9,237	  6,835   26,364    18,798</p>
<p> Interest expense     (1,144)	(1,119)  (3,792)   (3,676)</p>
<p> Other - net		  719	    638    2,066     1,469</p>
<p>Income before</p>
<p>   income taxes	   8,812	  6,354   24,638    16,591</p>
<p>Income tax (provision)</p>
<p>   benefit		  3,200	  5,700	---     7,000</p>
<p> Net income		 5,612	 12,054   24,638    23,591</p>
<p>Net income per share</p>
<p>  of common stock	  0.39	   0.83     1.70	1.63</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said the prior year Q3 includes an income tax benefit of $8 million, or $0.55/shr, recorded principally to recognize, for financial reporting purposes, the benefit of certain net operating loss carry forwards.</p>
<p>The income tax provision/benefit figures in the table for prior yr Q3 is the net benefit recognized after provision for taxes.</p>
<p>---New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
